# Set these in your request client's private environment. Do not save live tokens here.
# On 503 write_capacity_exceeded, honor Retry-After and keep the original body/key.
@API_BASE = https://localhost:8443
@ACCESS_TOKEN = <trusted-access-token>
@FORUM_ID = <provisioned-forum-uuid>
@TOPIC_ID = <created-topic-uuid>
@ROOT_ID = <root-message-uuid>
@QUOTE_ID = <same-topic-message-uuid>
@CREATE_REQUEST_ID = <new-uuid-reuse-on-retry>
@REPLY_REQUEST_ID = <another-uuid-reuse-on-retry>

### Current local identity
GET {{API_BASE}}/v1/me
Authorization: Bearer {{ACCESS_TOKEN}}

### OpenAPI 3.2.1; info.version=0.4.5
GET {{API_BASE}}/openapi.json

### Independent member forum
GET {{API_BASE}}/v1/forums/{{FORUM_ID}}
Authorization: Bearer {{ACCESS_TOKEN}}

### Create a threaded topic; copy topic.id to TOPIC_ID
POST {{API_BASE}}/v1/forums/{{FORUM_ID}}/topics
Authorization: Bearer {{ACCESS_TOKEN}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: {{CREATE_REQUEST_ID}}

{"title":"Independent forum fixture","body":"Opening message","mode":"threaded"}

### Seek pagination; follow the opaque next value as the after query parameter
GET {{API_BASE}}/v1/forums/{{FORUM_ID}}/topics?limit=37
Authorization: Bearer {{ACCESS_TOKEN}}

### Topic metadata
GET {{API_BASE}}/v1/topics/{{TOPIC_ID}}
Authorization: Bearer {{ACCESS_TOKEN}}

### A root reply; omit root_id to create a root, copy its id to ROOT_ID
POST {{API_BASE}}/v1/topics/{{TOPIC_ID}}/messages
Authorization: Bearer {{ACCESS_TOKEN}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: {{REPLY_REQUEST_ID}}

{"body":"Root reply"}

### Same-topic quote and one nested level; use a fresh request UUID
POST {{API_BASE}}/v1/topics/{{TOPIC_ID}}/messages
Authorization: Bearer {{ACCESS_TOKEN}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: <new-uuid-for-this-different-request>

{"body":"Reply with a precise message reference","root_id":"{{ROOT_ID}}","quote_id":"{{QUOTE_ID}}"}

### Authorized history; position/sequence values are JSON strings
GET {{API_BASE}}/v1/topics/{{TOPIC_ID}}/messages?limit=37
Authorization: Bearer {{ACCESS_TOKEN}}

### Bodyless POST; refresh this credential when requested by the SDK
POST {{API_BASE}}/v1/realtime/connection-token
Authorization: Bearer {{ACCESS_TOKEN}}

### Bodyless POST returns a channel descriptor, not a subscription token
POST {{API_BASE}}/v1/topics/{{TOPIC_ID}}/subscription
Authorization: Bearer {{ACCESS_TOKEN}}

### Forum-level topic-created events
POST {{API_BASE}}/v1/forums/{{FORUM_ID}}/subscription
Authorization: Bearer {{ACCESS_TOKEN}}
